  "worked_solution": "The area bounded by a polar curve is given by\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{{\\theta }_{1}}^{{\\theta }_{2}}{r}^{2}(\\theta )\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\n$$\n\nWhen $r(\\theta )=3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3\\theta )$, ${\\theta }_{1}=\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ and ${\\theta }_{2}=\\pi $, this gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{\\pi }{(3\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3\\theta ))}^{2}\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 9{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}\u2061(3\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{2}{\\int }_{2\\pi /3}^{\\pi }{sin}^{2}\u2061(3\\theta )\\,\\text{d}\\theta \\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
